{"kind":"request","text":"hugh: retire the artifacts recorded at comma-joined pseudo-paths. AGENTS.md already sanctions this — it says those artifacts have the same defect as the whole-repository artifacts at `.` and take the same repair, under their own request — so this is that request rather than a proposal.\nMeasured against main 4f8d06a0: thirty-three artifacts name a path containing a comma; twenty-five are still live. Fifteen are mine and all fifteen are stale; ten are codex's, four of them stale. Eighty-four records rest directly on one of them.\nWhy it matters, in the terms AGENTS.md sets: paths match as exact strings, so a comma-joined string is one path that no real predecessor and no real successor can ever equal. It flares nothing and nothing flares it. Forty-one distinct real paths are buried inside these twenty-five strings, and twenty-one of those forty-one carry no live artifact of their own — including internal/service/server.go, internal/nexus/nexus.go, internal/workroom/schema.go and internal/service/uidist. For those, the pseudo-path artifact is the only pointer there is, and it is a pointer nothing can supersede. A merge touching internal/nexus today supersedes nothing anchored there and the documentation resting on it cannot flare, however far the code moves.\nAddressed to you because of authority, not preference. The fold admits a supersession only from the target's own author or an actor holding ratifier. codex and I are bare participants, so each of us can retire only our own; you are the one actor who can retire the whole set in one run, exactly as the `.` migration says. I can retire my fifteen unilaterally and will if you would rather split it, but that leaves the set half-repaired and the codex ten standing.\nNot started, and deliberately so. The `.` procedure says to wait for a quiet wave, because retirement is retroactive and gs merge refuses a stale approval. It is not quiet right now: codex's test-lane head 515cf306 is carrying my changes-requested verdict and is waiting on your ratification of proposal 31ffb2ba, and one of these pseudo-paths — go.mod,cmd,internal,spike,Makefile,README.md,docs/reference.md,ui/vite.config.ts — covers Makefile and cmd, which that head changes. Retiring it mid-flight could stale work that is about to be re-reviewed.\nSuggested order, if you agree: ratify or decline 31ffb2ba and let the test lane land first, then run the retirement as one gs batch, then publish first artifacts at the real paths that have none. I am happy to do the survey and generate the batch file for you to sign; what I cannot do is sign it.","body":{"conditions":"Every live artifact whose path contains a comma is retired by a bare supersession naming the real path or paths the area will use; no successor is ever published at a comma-joined string; each real path that had no live artifact of its own and still carries behaviour gets a first artifact; the retirement runs when no approved head is waiting to merge.","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}